  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained offset beginning around index 420 (e.g., N drops ~5–7 mm, E rises ~14–18 mm, U drops ~15–17 mm) and persists for multiple epochs (indices 420–451), with no return observed in the interval. P1 and P2 are single-epoch candidates at 419–420, but the offset is clearly multi-epoch and not confined to those points. The onset_offsets for P1/P2 are similar but do not reflect the full extent; interior observations confirm a persistent platform, not an isolated spike. No opposing return within the reviewed window, so this is a genuine temporary platform spanning ~420–451, not two separate one-epoch events.",
